From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:36:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: let the time bound end the drain after the data
 phase

Stopping during a download ended in status=-110 at "branch 5" and a firmware
restart, on 4 of 5 cycles before and now on one of three roams under transfer.
After the data phase the worker drains the receive path until the frames still
in flight have their status, bounded by 64 reads, 256 KiB or 750 ms. A download
uses the 64 reads in about 7 ms, with 11 frames still owed. A transmit alone
does not.

Let the 750 ms bound decide, with the other two raised well past what it allows.

Part of the Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 4.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac-priv.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac-priv.h b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac-priv.h
index 3a0d7a942..4f22cb65f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac-priv.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac-priv.h
@@ -178,9 +178,9 @@ struct mt6797_join_rearm_state {
  * its own finite ceiling, set below the parent command/frame/grant/lifetime
  * deadlines, after which an unretired ledger fails through the normal terminal.
  */
-#define MT6797_NATIVE_DIAG_RETIRE_READS 64U            /* further all-class reads */
+#define MT6797_NATIVE_DIAG_RETIRE_READS 16384U /* further all-class reads */
 
-#define MT6797_NATIVE_DIAG_RETIRE_BYTES (256U * 1024U) /* 256 KiB drained */
+#define MT6797_NATIVE_DIAG_RETIRE_BYTES (16U * 1024U * 1024U) /* 16 MiB drained */
 
 #define MT6797_NATIVE_DIAG_RETIRE_MS    750U           /* below the parent deadlines */
 
